  "summary": "Your messages queue is clear: 8 items closed, including one that came in while I was working. All were decided under RBC-RX-05. Three results arrived at 08:00 and changed decisions I'd already made. I corrected those orders, sent the patients corrected messages and documented why in each chart.\n\n**Need your review (refills held; urgent tasks to you)**\n- **Samuel Price (pt-0030), lisinopril 20 mg:** No refill. The lab corrected the 10/06 creatinine from 1.36 to 1.49. That's 35% above the 1.10 he had before the 09/18 dose increase, which the protocol treats as potassium ≥5.5. I'd already placed a 90-day refill on the original value (mr-t0001) and cancelled it before it was dispensed. Task task-t0023 is on mr-00295, which now shows as stopped only because the cancelled order replaced it. He says his 20 mg supply has run out.\n- **Frank Odum (pt-0027), lisinopril 10 mg:** No refill. The August outside potassium of 5.9 didn't count because the sample was hemolyzed, so I first renewed for 90 days (mr-t0003) and ordered a repeat BMP (sr-t0006). Then an outside St. Brigid BMP from 10/20 arrived with a valid potassium of 5.8. I cancelled mr-t0003 before it was dispensed. Task task-t0024 is on mr-00283, which also shows stopped only because the cancelled order replaced it. The repeat BMP order sr-t0006 is still active; keep or cancel it.\n- **Leonard Kaplan (pt-0070), lisinopril 20 mg:** No refill. His 10/19 creatinine was 1.46, 46% above the 1.00 from the morning of the 09/28 dose increase. That evening's urgent care value (1.24, with dehydration) was drawn after the increase, so it isn't the baseline. Order mr-70002 is unchanged; task task-t0008 is on it.\n\n**Refilled**\n- **Samuel Price, metformin 1000 mg twice daily:** 90 days, 1 refill (mr-t0002). The corrected eGFR is 58; his HbA1c of 7.1% from an outside lab was drawn 08/19. That one order covers his portal request and both pharmacy requests.\n- **Marcus Webb (pt-0031), metformin 500 mg twice daily:** 90 days, 1 refill (mr-t0005). His eGFR is 92 and HbA1c 6.9% (both 09/28). The 10/14 eGFR of 39 was marked entered in error (mislabelled specimen).\n- **Marcus Webb, lisinopril 10 mg:** First a 30-day supply with a BMP order, because the last BMP on file was more than 12 months old. A BMP from 10/22 then arrived (potassium 4.6), so I replaced that with a 90-day supply, 1 refill (mr-t0022).\n\n**One thing for you to do:** Webb's BMP order (sr-t0007) is now redundant, and I couldn't cancel a lab order with the tools I have. Task task-t0025 asks you to cancel it.\n\nI've left the three 08:00 results open in your results queue (inbox-a0001, a0003, a0004) for your own sign-off, along with your other results items.",
